ponential-before-congr", :offer/hook "Reaching the library's one-sided complex-exponential integrals — `integral_exp_mul_complex_Ioi` / `_Iic` and their `integrableOn_` partners — requires the integrand to be LITERALLY `Complex.exp (a * ↑x)` with `a : ℂ` a constant, but what you have is a product: an oscillatory phase `Complex.exp (↑(c * x * w) * Complex.I)` times a cast real decay `((Real.exp (d * x) : ℝ) : ℂ)`. Applying `congr 1` to that product cannot work — it would have to match the two factors separately, which they never do — and the error it reports is a cast-of-a-compound versus compound-of-casts mismatch, so it reads as a coercion problem and you re-run `push_cast` instead of changing the shape. Fuse the two exponentials FIRST: `rw [Complex.ofReal_exp, ← Complex.exp_add]`, then state the equality of the two exponential ARGUMENTS as a standalone `have` closed by `congr 1; push_cast; ring`, and rewrite the goal with that `have`. Only after the fusion is `congr 1` acting on `Complex.exp _ = Complex.exp _`, where it is exactly the right tactic.", :pattern "math-formalization-CA/measure-integration-api"} {:pattern-hook nil, :route :sibling, :hops 1, :memory-id "e-codexpilot-apply-radial-R3-integration-through-a-one-dimensional-profile", :offer/name "apply-radial-R3-integration-through-a-one-dimensional-profile", :offer/hook "For norm-radial functions on `R³`, route through the reusable radial reduction before rebuilding polar-coordinate measure theory in the problem file.", :pattern "math-formalization-CA/measure-integration-api"} {:pattern-hook nil, :route :sibling, :hops 1, :memory-id "e-codexpilot-avoid-euclidean-measurable-space-diamond-by-direct-general-instantiation", :offer/name "avoid-euclidean-measurable-space-diamond-by-direct-general-instantiation", :offer/hook "When chaining a specialization exposes an instance diamond, return to the general theorem and instantiate its measure and function explicitly at the use site.", :pattern "math-formalization-CA/measure-integration-api"} {:pattern-hook nil, :route :sibling, :hops 1, :memory-id "e-codexpilot-build-an-Orlicz-bound-counterexample-from-a-borderline-power-singularity", :offer/name "build-an-Orlicz-bound-counterexample-from-a-borderline-power-singularity", :offer/hook "For entropy-controlled counterexamples, choose a singularity whose failed target norm becomes a standard borderline power, and use a nearby integrable power only to dominate the logarithmic entropy term.", :pattern "math-formalization-CA/measure-integration-api"} {:pattern-hook nil, :route :sibling, :hops 1, :memory-id "e-codexpilot-complete-diskwise-L1-to-compact-uniform-convergence-on-local-half-disks", :offer/name "complete-diskwise-L1-to-compact-uniform-convergence-on-local-half-disks", :offer/hook "When a convergence hypothesis is local on disks, prove uniform Cauchy convergence and pointwise identification on one smaller concentric disk at a time, then use the local-uniform API for compact globalization.", :pattern "math-formalization-CA/measure-integration-api"} {:pattern-hook nil, :route :sibling, :hops 1, :memory-id "e-codexpilot-derive-a-sinc-tail-identity-by-differentiating-cosine-over-x", :offer/name "derive-a-sinc-tail-identity-by-differentiating-cosine-over-x", :offer/hook "For an oscillatory `sin x/x` tail, differentiate `cos x/x`: the resulting integrable `cos x/x²` remainder isolates the decaying boundary terms.", :pattern "math-formalization-CA/measure-integration-api"} {:pattern-hook nil, :route :sibling, :hops 1, :memory-id "e-codexpilot-derive-improper-integrability-from-a-monotone-antiderivative-limit", :offer/name "derive-improper-integrability-from-a-monotone-antiderivative-limit", :offer/hook "When evaluating a nonnegative improper integral, prefer an FTC theorem that derives integrability from a finite antiderivative limit over a route that first assumes or separately reconstructs Bochner integrability.", :pattern "math-formalization-CA/measure-integration-api"} {:patter